{
    "background_story": "Jamison was a introspective poet who spent most of his days lost in thought. He had a habit of ruminate on life's big questions, often getting caught up in his own musings. While others saw him as aloof or distant, Jamison was simply processing the world around him. He'd spend hours sitting by the lake, watching the water lap against the shore, and pondering the mysteries of existence. His friends would often joke that he was 'chewing his cud' like a cow, but Jamison didn't mind. He knew that his ruminations were the source of his creativity, and that they fueled his writing. As he sat on the lake's edge, he'd scribble down lines of poetry, capturing the essence of his thoughts and emotions. Jamison's rumination was his superpower, allowing him to craft words that touched the hearts of all who read them.",
